{
  "_comment": [
    "Sunrise Izumo / Sunrise Seto — Japan's last scheduled sleeper, read by scripts/adapters/jr-sunrise.mjs.",
    "This file is the BASELINE the nightly scrape falls back to and checks itself against: stop patterns, positions, the drawn line, and the fare tariff. The adapter refreshes the times of every stop and the berth charges from JR West's own pages each night; a page that does not validate costs tonight's refresh, never the train.",
    "Times left null are ones no source this file was written from states reliably. They stay blank until a scrape reads them from JR's timetable (a blank beats an invented time).",
    "Stop patterns are asymmetric on purpose: the westbound train serves Hamamatsu and does NOT stop at Osaka or Sannomiya for passengers; the Tokyo-bound train serves Sannomiya and Osaka and does NOT stop at Hamamatsu. Neither direction serves Neu. The two trains run coupled between Tokyo and Okayama.",
    "Not modelled: Sunrise Seto's extension to Kotohira on selected dates, and the seasonal Sunrise Izumo 91/92 extras."
  ],
