  "fares": {
    "_comment": [
      "Per traveller, whole route, one way. A class price = basic fare + limited express charge + berth charge.",
      "`ticketAndSleeperExpress` is the basic fare plus the limited express charge a sleeper passenger pays (the same all year). It is JR's distance tariff, so it changes only at a fare revision — which is why it is curated here rather than scraped. Figures as quoted for 2026: Tokyo–Izumoshi Single 23,210 yen and Tokyo–Takamatsu Single 22,650 yen, each less the 7,700 yen Single charge. JR East's 14 March 2026 revision added a JR East supplement to through fares that start or end on its lines; if JR's own fare search disagrees, correct these two numbers.",
      "The Nobinobi carpet space needs no berth charge but pays the reserved-seat limited express charge instead, which is the sleeper one plus `seatExpressPremium` in the regular season (200 yen less off-peak, 200-400 yen more at peak).",
      "`roomCharges` are refreshed nightly from JR West's pages by the adapter. Sunrise Twin is per ROOM; its per-person price assumes two people share it."
    ],
